      "problem": "Solve the equation $\\frac{7w+10}{3}=4w.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7w+10}{3} & =4w \\\\ 3(\\frac{7w+10}{3}) & =3\\cdot (4w) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{7w+10}{\\cancel{3}}) & =12w \\\\ 7w+10 & =12w\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7w+10 & =12w \\\\ 7w+10-7w & =12w-7w \\\\ 10 & =5w \\\\ \\frac{10}{5} & =\\frac{5w}{5} \\\\ 2 & =w\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $w=2.$",
